.Dd November 14, 2026
.Dt LOGTOPF 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm logtopf
.Nd live terminal view of the packets pf logs
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl h
.Op Fl B Ar buffer_size
.Op Ar interface
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads the packets
.Xr pf 4
logs to a
.Xr pflog 4
interface and shows them as a live table of flows, with packet, byte and
rate counters.
Only traffic matched by rules with the
.Cm log
keyword appears, so the view stays focused on what was asked for.
.Pp
The
.Ar interface
defaults to
.Pa pflog0 .
Reading it needs root, or read access to
.Pa /dev/bpf .
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl B Ar buffer_size
Ask for a kernel capture buffer of
.Ar buffer_size
KiB instead of the default 4096.
The kernel grants at most
.Va net.bpf.maxbufsize ,
and
.Nm
warns at startup when it got less than this asked for.
.It Fl h
Print a short usage message and exit.
.El
.Pp
Each row is a flow, keyed by source, destination, protocol, port, action
and direction.
The port is the lower of the source and destination ports, which is the
service port for nearly all traffic.
Rates are bytes per second over a two second window.
Addresses on the subnets of the machine's own interfaces are highlighted.
.Sh KEYS
.Bl -tag -width "Left, Right" -compact
.It Ic Up , Down
Scroll.
.It Ic Left , Right
Change the sort column.
.It Ic s
Reverse the sort order.
.It Ic x
Clear the flow table.
.It Ic r
Toggle hostname resolution.
.It Ic p
Toggle port names.
.It Ic c
Toggle colour.
.It Ic i
Toggle highlighting of local addresses.
.It Ic u
Toggle between 1024-based and 1000-based units.
.It Ic 3 , 4
Toggle counting of IP and of TCP and UDP header bytes.
.It Ic Ctrl-L
Repaint the whole screen.
.It Ic \&? , h
Show the keys.
.It Ic q
Quit.
.El
.Sh STATUS LINE
.Bl -tag -width "KRN" -compact
.It Cm RX
Packets received from the interface.
.It Cm BUF
How full the buffer between the capture and worker threads is.
.It Cm KRN
Packets the kernel dropped because its capture buffer was full.
If this grows, raise
.Va net.bpf.maxbufsize
and use
.Fl B ;
see
.Xr bpf 4 .
.It Cm APP
Packets dropped because the worker thread made no progress for two seconds.
Should stay at 0.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Log incoming web traffic for every packet of the connection, and blocked
packets on the outside interface:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
pass in log (all) on $lan proto tcp to port { 80 443 }
block in log on $wan
.Ed
.Pp
Plain
.Cm log
records only the packet that creates a state.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr bpf 4 ,
.Xr pf 4 ,
.Xr pflog 4 ,
.Xr pf.conf 5 ,
.Xr pfctl 8 ,
.Xr pflogd 8
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Timon Durot
